 leans Democratic by about 2 points on PVI"], "rationale": "Every major rater calls this Safe or Solid D, markets price Davids near 96%, and her fundraising advantage over Jenkins is roughly ninety-to-one. With no contrary polling, the fundamentals-based margin of about 15 points stands.", "watch": "A late surge of Republican outside spending or an unexpectedly strong national GOP environment could narrow the margin, though not likely enough to threaten the seat.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Sharice Davids (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Sharice Davids seeks another term in Kansas' 3rd District, a suburban-leaning seat that favors Democrats by about two points. She faces Republican Eric Jenkins and Libertarian Steven Hohe in November. Davids has raised about $4.7 million and holds $1.9 million on hand, while Jenkins has raised roughly $52,000, leaving him little capacity to introduce himself to voters.\n\nNo general-election polling is available, but the expert consensus is unanimous: ten raters place the race at Safe or Solid D, and prediction markets give Davids about a 96% chance of winning. With a strong incumbent, a lopsided money advantage, and no evidence of a competitive race, the forecast points to a comfortable Davids re-election.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9826, "margin": 15.09}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9781, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9789, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.979, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.97, "margin": 14.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9714, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9748, "margin": 14.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9784, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9769, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9798, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9747, "margin": 15